  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Missouri has recorded $396M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Award activity includes 11,264 awards with an average award size of $35.2K. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. Historical context shows larger annual totals: FY22 totaled $11.4B, FY23 totaled $16B, FY24 totaled $17B, FY25 totaled $14.5B, and FY26 totaled $13.1B. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer so far in FY2027, with obligations of $321M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligation, totaling $324M. HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC is the largest vendor by obligation, totaling $323M. The remaining top buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs with $23.4M and the Department of Homeland Security with $12.6M. Other notable industry and vendor pockets of spending include Office Administrative Services at $11.6M and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC at $11.4M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
