        "heading": "Which agencies are driving federal obligations in Missouri, FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $321M, making it the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $23.4M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $12.6M. Remaining top buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $11.3M and the Department of Justice at $10.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries capture the most federal dollars in Missouri, FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC captured $323M, making it the largest vendor by obligations. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $324M. Other leading vendors include KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC at $11.4M and ENVIRONMENTAL QUALITY MANAGEMENT, INC at $8.8M, while Office Administrative Services totaled $11.6M in obligations."
      }
    ]
